  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% acc, far outperforming image (resnet50, singleprofile) at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. However, we have only one RNA data point, so we cannot yet tell whether multiprofile aggregation improves the RNA signal. Question: Does switching from singleprofile to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation improve RNA performance while keeping the same pca_n2000 encoder? This isolates the profile/aggregation axis as the only change from config_001. Why best next: It is the minimal logical extension of our best result, directly tests a design axis (profile setting + aggregation) that gates ~half the remaining configuration space, and its outcome will inform whether to invest subsequent budget in multiprofile variants or focus on encoder choice. A single-variable change keeps the comparison clean and interpretable under a tight budget."
}

